dy-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:d96421371cd573ece0e72b381e42f01cef64cf6602ef5b598eba6c50625b51b0","file":"preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex","line":77,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"664009c4d778b57690238557d14a90c75777b778ab900292dd005e9e22177277","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d96421371cd573ece0e72b381e42f01cef64cf6602ef5b598eba6c50625b51b0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex#L77"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:nonclique-dynamics}\nSuppose $M$ is irreducible, meaning that there is no nontrivial partition\n$S=S_1\\sqcup S_2$ with $m_{st}=2$ for every $s\\in S_1$, $t\\in S_2$, and\nsuppose $m_{st}=\\infty$ for some pair. Then $A$ is acylindrically hyperbolic.\nEvery proper parabolic subgroup $P$ has a conjugate meeting it trivially:\nthere is $g\\in A$ such that $P\\cap gPg^{-1}=\\{1\\}$."}
